      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249809/assets/3d77350a21cc1cd9fa6ab59222ac451d252e9d608720496e2e2f3a5f7f770fc4.png)\n\nGiven $△ABC$ shown above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AC}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AC}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $B$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{AC},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{AC}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{AC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249809/assets/2733f933e3626c4de2472331574975777bbc7c7bd5f6e6aa5f0a1359d9a07e55.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $B$ to $\\overset{⟷}{AC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249809/assets/b7dcabe286cdd4961d8a719e60d23e0e2b772c316cb799b4a3c649237f0ee345.png)",
